{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI write from Cologne, though my feet have been in Koblenz and Bonn. The weather turned foul, forcing me into a boat rather than a carriage. I visited the Moravian Sisters in Neuwied; their quiet discipline struck me as a small, orderly world, very different from our chaotic streets. In Bonn, I called on Windischmann and his son-in-law, Walther. The conversation was lively, as usual, though I confess I was tired by the journey. I stopped at Linz to see a painting Schulze had raved about; it was decent, but I would rather have had a glass of wine and a quiet room.\n\nI am well, if somewhat damp. The Rhine is wide and grey tonight. I think of you and the boys in Berlin. Please do not worry about my health; I am merely a bit weary. I look forward to returning to my study and my whist partners.\n\nYour loving husband,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080197,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":207,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1159,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-XYwbNoCR0Z84SFrThESrSQvFZ6vaWdT8","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":892.707,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9377174369747899,"prompt_per_second":1066.4193290743772,"predicted_n":207,"predicted_ms":4926.647,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.91576213592233,"predicted_per_second":41.81342807796053}}